// Deal or Force - where an army is standing when the scenario opens.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Why this file exists
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Every division in the game is dealt into a ring around its own capital. For a country at
// peace that is a fair answer and nobody notices. For the two countries the scenario is
// actually about it is the wrong one: the front runs across eastern Ukraine and both armies
// begin a thousand kilometres behind it, near Moscow and near Kyiv. The line is drawn and
// nobody is standing on it, so the opening weeks are two armies walking towards a front that
// anybody could have taken while they marched.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What a row means
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//     share       what fraction of that country's divisions start forward. The rest stay
//                 at the capital, which is where a country's reserves and its garrison are.
//     positions   where they stand, [longitude, latitude] in degrees. Divisions are dealt
//                 round-robin along the list, and each pass out rings the place it lands on,
//                 so a long list reads as a front and a short one as a concentration.
//
// The coordinates below are the contact line as it stood on 1 January 2024 and the border
// north of it, each side on its own ground - which was checked against the scenario's own
// ownership map rather than assumed, because half of these places changed hands in 2022 and
// the file would otherwise be putting armies inside each other.
{
  // Russia keeps rather less than half its army forward: the rest is the garrison of a
  // country eleven time zones wide, and that is roughly the shape of it in 2024.
  "RUS": {
    "share": 0.45,
    "positions": [
      [38.15, 49.41],   // Svatove
      [38.23, 49.05],   // Kreminna
      [38.00, 48.60],   // Bakhmut
      [37.75, 48.14],   // Avdiivka
      [37.30, 47.60],   // north of Mariupol
      [36.60, 47.20],   // Melitopol approaches
      [34.60, 47.05],   // the Dnipro bend
      [36.59, 50.60],   // Belgorod, over the border
      [38.10, 50.21],   // Valuyki
      [36.19, 51.73],   // Kursk
      [34.37, 52.25],   // Bryansk
      [38.90, 47.21]    // Taganrog
    ]
  },

  // Ukraine keeps almost everything forward, because almost everything it has is on this
  // line and the rest of the country has nobody to garrison against.
  "UKR": {
    "share": 0.75,
    "positions": [
      [37.62, 49.71],   // Kupiansk
      [37.50, 47.94],   // Marinka
      [36.86, 47.83],   // Velyka Novosilka
      [35.79, 47.57],   // Orikhiv
      [35.83, 47.44],   // Robotyne
      [32.62, 46.64],   // Kherson, on the west bank
      [36.23, 49.99],   // Kharkiv
      [35.05, 48.47],   // Dnipro
      [35.14, 47.84],   // Zaporizhzhia
      [34.80, 50.91],   // Sumy
      [31.29, 51.50]    // Chernihiv
    ]
  }
}
